WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.490
This is a book saying
there are black people

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.520
who need help, and the people

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.382
who are calling themselves
black people saviors now

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:09.300
don't understand this,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.780
but they're hurting black people,

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.900
because what they're caught up in

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.008
is more about virtue
signaling to one another

00:00:15.008 --> 00:00:17.510
than helping people
who actually need help.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.040
In his bestselling new book, "Woke Racism,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.100
How a New Religion has
Betrayed Black America,"

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.270
New York Times columnist and
Columbia University linguist,

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.411
John McWhorter argues that
the ideas of Robin Diangelo,

00:00:29.411 --> 00:00:33.000
Ibram X. Kendi, and the 1619 Project

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.237
undermine blacks by
sharpening racial divides

00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:39.940
and distracting from actual
obstacles to real progress.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.370
Reason spoke with the
56-year-old McWhorter

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.570
about what whites get out of cooperating

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.710
with an ideological agenda
that cast them as devils,

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.190
what blacks gained by
performing victim-hood,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.690
and what needs to change,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.840
so that all Americans can get on

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.757
with creating a more perfect union.

